</figure>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S3.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.05625v1/Attack_Qualiative.png" id="S3.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/355;" width="685" height="355" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S3.F4.sf1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative Comparison across 6 methods for the CCE attack.<span id="S3.F4.sf1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Both E-CEM methods, CA and MACE, are vulnerable to the CCE attack. STEREO’s erasure is too aggressive, leaving only Van Gogh-style elements, with this concept being easier to erase. Our method defends against CCE by mapping the target concept to its reference concept.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S3.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.05625v1/Textual_Qualiative.png" id="S3.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/353;" width="685" height="353" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S3.F4.sf2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative Comparison across 6 methods for image generation.<span id="S3.F4.sf2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> CA struggles with ”English Springer” and ”Elon Musk.” MACE performs well, preserving image quality. RACE shows slight degradation, and STEREO significantly reduces quality. Our method strikes a balance between E-CEMs and C-CEMs in terms of quality.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S3.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative Results.<span id="S3.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We present qualitative results comparing five methods against the CCE attack and textual erasure.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Proposed Method</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our framework, <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">SuMa</span>, consists of two stages, as illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3 Method ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The first stage, termed <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subspace Construction</span>, aims to identify Textual Inversion tokens to establish both sets of Target Subspace <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{U}^{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{U}^{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and Reference Subspace <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{V}^{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{V}^{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th subspace (corresponding to <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th Unet layer) of the concept to be erased, while <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th the subspace into which we intend to map our <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th target subspace. In the second stage, <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subspace Elimination</span>, we refine the to-<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and to-<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> weights of the Cross-Attention Layer in U-Net, denoted as <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing us to project the basis of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to the identical functionality of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> in our work, we denote both as <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity and readability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subspace Construction.</span> Starting with the original model, denoted as <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and a concept to be removed, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply a Concept Ablation (<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>) to eliminate <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in a modified model <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. This process is repeated over <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> steps. At <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration, we apply Textual Inversion (TI) for the concept to be erased from <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding two tokens: one from the final step of TI training, denoted as <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u\rangle_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u\rangle_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and another from an earlier step, denoted as <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v\rangle_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v\rangle_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Subsequently, we construct prompts in the formats <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”A photo of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u\rangle_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u\rangle_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>”</span> and <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”A photo of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v\rangle_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v\rangle_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>”</span>, which are then passed through the Text Encoder <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> to extract embeddings for the tokens <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. We then apply the transformation <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> represent <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer in Unet, to these extracted embeddings, treating the outputs as <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as basis vectors for the subspaces
<math id="S3.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> respestively. Formally, this process is defined as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\langle u^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}&amp;=W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}(p+\langle u\rangle_{j}),\\
\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}&amp;=W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}(p+\langle v\rangle_{j}),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\langle u^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}&amp;=W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}(p+\langle u\rangle_{j}),\\
\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{j}^{i}&amp;=W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}(p+\langle v\rangle_{j}),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> represents the prompt template. Finally, we fine-tune <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> to remove <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle u_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle u_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in an updated model <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> at the end of each iteration (Fig. <a href="#S3.F3.sf1" title="Figure 3(a) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 3 Method ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(a)</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subspace Elimination.</span> Fig. <a href="#S3.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 3 Method ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a> illustrates this process. After constructing sets of the subspaces <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{U}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{U}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{V}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{V}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is number of layer in Unet, our goal is to eliminate all <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by fine-tuning <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> so that the basis vectors of <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are projected onto <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. To construct the projection matrix onto <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first define the matrix <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{i}=[\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{1}^{i},\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{2}^{i},\dots,\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{l}^{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{i}=[\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{1}^{i},\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{2}^{i},\dots,\langle v^{\prime}\rangle_{l}^{i}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times l}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the dimension of token embedding vector, and the projection matrix <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> can then be formulated as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}=\mathbf{V}^{i}\left(\left(\mathbf{V}^{i}\right)^{T}\mathbf{V}^{i}\right)^{-1}\left(\mathbf{V}^{i}\right)^{T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}=\mathbf{V}^{i}\left(\left(\mathbf{V}^{i}\right)^{T}\mathbf{V}^{i}\right)^{-1}\left(\mathbf{V}^{i}\right)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{proj}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{proj}</annotation></semantics></math> as the objective to project all basis of <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by following formula:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{proj}=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\sum_{j=1}^{l}\left\|W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle u\rangle_{j}\right)-\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle u\rangle_{j}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>l</mi></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{proj}=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\sum_{j=1}^{l}\left\|W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle u\rangle_{j}\right)-\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle u\rangle_{j}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">As per <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, we add a regulization term to keep the <span id="S3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Reference Subspace</span> <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged during fine-tuning:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{reg}=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\sum_{j=1}^{l}\left\|W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle v\rangle_{j}\right)-\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle v\rangle_{j}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>l</mi></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{reg}=\sum_{i=1}^{M}\sum_{j=1}^{l}\left\|W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle v\rangle_{j}\right)-\mathbf{P}_{\mathbf{V}^{i}}W_{k}^{i}\mathcal{T}\left(p+\langle v\rangle_{j}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The objective function for subspace mapping, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{sub}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{sub}</annotation></semantics></math>, is then defined as the weighted sum of these two terms:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{sub}=L_{proj}+\lambda_{reg}L_{reg}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{sub}=L_{proj}+\lambda_{reg}L_{reg},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{reg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{reg}</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperparameter (default 1). If we use <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{sub}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{sub}</annotation></semantics></math> to fine-tune <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and use CCE to find a new target token, this token still generates the target concept when conditioned on <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, but not on <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> (see Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Modify Cross-Attn Only ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>). We assume modifying only the cross-attention layer is effective for erasing a token, as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, but affects the SDE trajectory when erasing multiple tokens. To mitigate this, we use the CA loss function and discuss our choice in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.
. In short, their objective is:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{CA}}=\mathbb{E}_{z_{t},c,t}\left[\|\Phi^{\prime}(z_{t},\mathcal{T}(p+c^{\prime}),t)-\Phi(z_{t},\mathcal{T}(p+c),t)\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>CA</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{CA}}=\mathbb{E}_{z_{t},c,t}\left[\|\Phi^{\prime}(z_{t},\mathcal{T}(p+c^{\prime}),t)-\Phi(z_{t},\mathcal{T}(p+c),t)\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the model to learn, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is pretrained, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is Text-Encoder, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is prompt template, <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is target concept, and <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is its general term (e.g., <span id="S3.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">grumpy cat</span> vs. <span id="S3.SS3.p5.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">cat</span>). Our objective is:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{*}_{k}=\operatorname*{argmin}_{W_{k}}\left(L_{\text{final}}\right)=\operatorname*{argmin}_{W_{k}}\left(L_{\text{CA}}+L_{\text{sub}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">argmin</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>final</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">argmin</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>CA</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sub</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{*}_{k}=\operatorname*{argmin}_{W_{k}}\left(L_{\text{final}}\right)=\operatorname*{argmin}_{W_{k}}\left(L_{\text{CA}}+L_{\text{sub}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;">
<div id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:219.4pt;height:212pt;vertical-align:-103.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-9.5pt,9.2pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;">
<table id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:238.5pt;">
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Method</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">CCE <math id="S4.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">UD <math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">FID <math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">CLIP <math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;" colspan="5"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Subclass</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SD </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#AD0000;">0.84 / <span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">0.83</span></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#AD0000;">0.74 / <span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">0.76</span></span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">17.04 / </span><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">16.95</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.33 / </span><span id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.3.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">0.32</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.3.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
