<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Results</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quantitative Results.</span> We average each metric from Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Experimental Setting ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> for each category and report the results in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. For all baselines, we ensure the erased model works well for erasing the textual prompt, and we report results for this trivial task in the Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Standard Test on the Target’s Textual Prompts ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>. For <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">completeness</span> evaluation, our method achieves an ASR score below 0.2 for all categories under both <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CCE</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UD</span> attacks. Compared to <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">STEREO</span>, our method has a slightly higher ASR score (0.02 to 0.14 higher), but within an acceptable range. <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RACE</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AdvUnlearn</span> show safety against the <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UD</span> attack in the Subclass, Artistic, and Instance categories but fail under Identity. This is due to the subtle facial features of human identity, which make this category more fine-grained and challenging. However, both fail under the <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CCE</span> attack, showing that protecting the model against <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CCE</span> is harder than <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UD</span>. The main reason is that <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RACE</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AdvUnlearn</span> erase adversarial tokens based on <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UnlearnDiff</span>, but these tokens don’t fully represent the target concept, protecting against <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UD</span> but not <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CCE</span>. <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DUO</span> works well for <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NSFW</span> concepts (results in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E NSFW Concept Erasure ‣ SuMa: A Subspace Mapping Approach for Robust and Effective Concept Erasure in Text-to-Image Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>) but fails for narrow concepts. For <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">effectiveness</span>, although <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">STEREO</span> performs well under both <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CCE</span> and <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UD</span>, image quality is significantly affected, resulting in an <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID</span> score roughly double that of other <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E-CEMs</span>, making it less effective. Our method, while not achieving a perfect ASR, achieves an <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID</span> score comparable to other <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E-CEMs</span> in the Subclass, Artistic, and Identity categories, outperforming <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CA</span> with an <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID</span> around 0.85 lower. We found that Instance category is harder to be erased, so we fine-tuned it for 750 steps, resulting in a higher <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FID</span> compared to the others, fine-tuned for 500 steps.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.05625v1/fid_asr_scores_combined_tmp.svg" id="S4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:672/336;" width="672" height="336"></object>
